Redeploy data-loss audit (2026-09-09)

Uploaded CSV url_source files are destroyed by every redeploy.

CreateSite.php:307 and EditSite.php:203 take the CSV with
FileUpload->disk('public')->directory('csv-uploads'), and CreateSite.php:508
stores the site's url_source as asset('storage/'.$filePath). The backend
re-fetches that URL on every round. The file lives in the container's
storage/app/public, and the dashboard compose declares one volume —
mysql_data:/var/lib/mysql. Nothing persists storage. So a deploy deletes the
file, url_source 404s, and every future round for that site fails with no
repair short of re-uploading.

Latent right now: no production site currently uses a CSV source. It is a
trapdoor under a shipped feature, not a live outage.

Fix: a named volume for storage/app/public in the dashboard compose. Needs the
volume declared on the Coolify resource too, so it is a deploy-time change
rather than a code-only one.

storage/logs is ephemeral for the same reason.

This is why the dashboard crash investigation had no forensics — laravel.log
was destroyed by the redeploy that appeared to fix it. Either give logs a
volume as well or ship them to stdout so Coolify keeps them.

AdminSeeder recreates a known-password super admin.

Not an overwrite — it is firstOrCreate on admin@crawler.test, so an existing
account is left alone. But if that user is ever deleted, the next deploy
silently brings it back with Hash::make('password') and email_verified_at set.
Worth dropping from DatabaseSeeder in production, or gating on
APP_ENV !== 'production'.

Seeders checked and safe: RoleSeeder (firstOrCreate on both roles),
PackageSeeder (now firstOrCreate on all four tiers — it previously overwrote
paid tiers on every deploy and reverted UI package edits).

Not at risk on redeploy: config/route/view caches regenerate, storage:link is
recreated by the entrypoint, MySQL has its volume, and Redis loss is already
covered by the orphan-recovery sweep.
